# Slot size per publish target, in bytes.
#
# A Data Tunnel publication registers a fixed message_size, and the Bridge cannot derive
# it from a payload it has not seen yet. The AuthzPolicy beside this file says WHAT may be
# published; this file says only how large the slot is registered. A payload that does not
# fit is dropped and counted, never truncated: a truncated protobuf would surface as a
# decode error far away from its cause.
#
# Format: <unit_type> <topic> <bytes>
# Both messages encode to at most six bytes plus a one-byte length; 64 leaves room without
# sending kilobytes of padding over the Data Tunnel for each command.
com.nexussdv.sample.PressureLimit pressure-limit 64
com.nexussdv.sample.DoorCommand door-command 64
# Room for a participant's payload; a larger one is dropped and counted.
com.nexussdv.sdk.Command command 1024
